# The annotations of the game image: the single source of truth for src/game/*.asm (kit/mkgame.py).
# The format is in kit/mkgame.py, class Annotations (docs/ann-format.md). Witness lines: "Witness: L1 N (builds)" counts
# the runs of the entry's first instruction in the recordings of case.json (tools/regen.sh --fix-witness).
@equ $4000 Screen 6144 ; the screen bitmap
@equ $5800 Attributes 768 ; the screen attributes
@equ $5B00 ParkedZone1 1280 ; zone 1's characters 0-159, parked: copied there from Zone1CharsLow $F000 at GameEntry
@equ $FE00 ImTable 257 ; the IM 2 vector table, all $FF (GameEntry)
@equ $FFF0 StackTop ; the stack top
@equ $FFF4 ImJump 3 ; JP Interrupt, written by GameEntry
@equ $FFFE MachineFlag ; 0 on a 128K (the loader found RAM 4), non-zero on a 48K
@equ $FFFF ImJr ; $18, the JR that sends the vector $FFFF to $FFF4
@bank $C000 MusicStart 4 ; the AY player: start tune A-1 (src/music/music.ann)
@bank $C003 MusicPlay 4 ; the AY player: one frame of the tune
@bank $C006 MusicTune 4 ; $FF while a tune runs from its start (MusicStart $C116), 0 when every channel has ended (MusicFrame $C12D / $C133) or MusicStop $C00B; the menu's interrupt restarts tune 1 when it is not $FF ($927E)
@bank $C00A MusicStop 4 ; the player: silence
@bank $C334 EffectChannelA 4 ; the player's effect block of channel A
@bank $C346 EffectChannelB 4 ; the effect block of channel B
@bank $C358 EffectChannelC 4 ; the effect block of channel C
@bank $C36A EffectStart 4 ; the player: start the effect of the block at IX
@isub $925B CALL MusicStart
@isub $9268 CALL MusicStop
@isub $9275 CALL MusicPlay
@isub $927E LD A,(MusicTune)
@isub $9285 CALL NZ,MusicStart
@isub $942B LD IX,EffectChannelA
@isub $943E JP EffectStart
@isub $944B LD IX,EffectChannelB
@isub $9460 LD IX,EffectChannelC
@isub $9476 LD (EffectChannelA+6),A
@isub $9486 LD (EffectChannelB+6),A
@isub $9495 LD (EffectChannelC+6),A
@isub $A1F2 LD (DirtyMap-1),A
@isub $A1F5 LD HL,DirtyMap+$0240
@isub $A593 LD DE,CharMap-$80
@isub $A688 LD BC,MaskBuffer
@isub $A70F LD DE,MaskBuffer
@isub $A779 LD DE,MaskBuffer
@isub $A853 LD BC,$FF00
@isub $A889 LD HL,BitReverse
@module zones ; The zone graphics: three parked sets of 256 characters and 256 attributes
@about MASK III draws every room from one of four zones' character sets (zone = room table byte 4: 0 the surface, 1 the caverns, 2 the moon, 3 the base). The live set is at ZoneChars $E000 (2048 bytes) and ZoneAttrs $EF00 (256 bytes, bit 7 = solid, IsSolid $B993); SwapZone $A198 swaps it byte for byte with a parked set at $5B00 + $900 x (slot - 1), ZoneSlots $A194 telling which zone sits where.
@about As loaded, zone 0 is live, zone 2 is parked at Zone2Chars $6400 and zone 3 at Zone3Chars $6D00. Zone 1's set at $5B00 is split by the loader, which itself lives at $5E00: its characters 160-255 are loaded here at Zone1CharsHigh $6000, characters 0-159 and the attributes wait at Zone1CharsLow $F000 and Zone1Attrs $EE00 until GameEntry $9100 copies them down.
@about The resources are PNG sheets of 16 characters a row (src/res/charsets/README.md) and the attributes as CSV.
$6000 b Zone1CharsHigh 8 ; Zone 1's characters 160-255 (768 bytes), parked in the set at $5B00
> Read by SwapZone $A198 when a room of zone 1 is drawn. Witness: the RZX segments reach the caverns (work/stage1/rec/rzx-*).
@res charsets/zone1-high.bin
$6300 b Zone1AttrsLeftover 16 ; 256 bytes overwritten at the entry by Zone1Attrs $EE00: an older copy of zone 1's attributes
> GameEntry $9100 copies Zone1Attrs $EE00 over these bytes before anything reads them; 255 of the 256 bytes equal the copy, only the first differs ($00 here, $47 at $EE00). Leftover, known only from the code.
@res leftovers/zone1-attrs-old.bin
$6400 b Zone2Chars 8 ; Zone 2's (the moon's) 256 characters, parked
@res charsets/zone2.bin
$6C00 b Zone2Attrs 16 ; Zone 2's attributes
@res charsets/zone2-attr.bin
$6D00 b Zone3Chars 8 ; Zone 3's 256 characters, parked
@res charsets/zone3.bin
$7500 b Zone3Attrs 16 ; Zone 3's attributes
@res charsets/zone3-attr.bin
@module rooms ; The rooms: 16 maps of 48 x 5 blocks, the 192 blocks of 4 x 4 characters
@about A room is a strip of six screens, 48 blocks across and 5 down, 240 bytes at Room0Map $7600 + 240 x room, stored row by row. A screen shows 8 block columns (32 characters); RoomScreen $950D holds 8 x the screen, the map column of its left edge. DrawRoom $A89D expands the screen's 8 x 5 blocks through Blocks $8500 (16 character codes a block, 4 rows of 4) into the character map $F080. The room table RoomTable $953B gives the exits, the zone and one enemy kind a screen.
@about The maps are also state: TakeBlockItem $B33D turns a taken item (block $1B) into block $47, KindTurret $C457 turns a dead turret's block $12 into $2B; NewGame $915B turns them back (every $2B into $12, every $47 into $1B). The resources are text grids (src/res/rooms/README.md); tools/roommap.py draws every room and the world map from them.
$7600 b Room0Map 48 ; Room 0: the surface (zone 0), the start, the password doors
@res rooms/room-00.bin
$76F0 b Room1Map 48 ; Room 1 (zone 0)
@res rooms/room-01.bin
$77E0 b Room2Map 48 ; Room 2 (zone 0)
@res rooms/room-02.bin
$78D0 b Room3Map 48 ; Room 3 (zone 0): the first code message
@res rooms/room-03.bin
$79C0 b Room4Map 48 ; Room 4 (zone 1)
@res rooms/room-04.bin
$7AB0 b Room5Map 48 ; Room 5 (zone 1)
@res rooms/room-05.bin
$7BA0 b Room6Map 48 ; Room 6 (zone 1)
@res rooms/room-06.bin
$7C90 b Room7Map 48 ; Room 7 (zone 2, the moon)
@res rooms/room-07.bin
$7D80 b Room8Map 48 ; Room 8 (zone 2)
@res rooms/room-08.bin
$7E70 b Room9Map 48 ; Room 9 (zone 2)
@res rooms/room-09.bin
$7F60 b Room10Map 48 ; Room 10 (zone 3)
@res rooms/room-10.bin
$8050 b Room11Map 48 ; Room 11 (zone 3)
@res rooms/room-11.bin
$8140 b Room12Map 48 ; Room 12 (zone 3)
@res rooms/room-12.bin
$8230 b Room13Map 48 ; Room 13 (zone 3)
@res rooms/room-13.bin
$8320 b Room14Map 48 ; Room 14 (zone 3)
@res rooms/room-14.bin
$8410 b Room15Map 48 ; Room 15 (zone 3): the last room, Scott at screen 5
@res rooms/room-15.bin
$8500 b Blocks 16 ; The 192 blocks: 16 character codes each, 4 rows of 4 (the codes index the live zone's set)
> Read by DrawRoom $A89D for every block of a screen ($A8E0-$A920). Witness: every room drawn in c1 and the RZX segments.
@res blocks/blocks.bin
@module entry ; The entry and the new game
@about LoaderMain jumps to GameEntry $9100 once the game and (on a 128K) the music are in. GameEntry completes the parked zone set, builds the IM 2 table and goes to GameStart $CBF9, which runs the menu and then a new game. NewGame $915B puts every piece of the world back: Matt, the energy, the mask slots, the pick-ups, the maps, the score.
$9100 c GameEntry ; The entry from the loader: the parked zone 1, IM 2, the Kempston test, then GameStart
> Copies Zone1CharsLow $F000 to $5B00 (1280 bytes) and Zone1Attrs $EE00 to $6300 (256), so that zone 1 is whole in the first parked slot; sets R = $FF (the random generator Random $92C6 reads R), SP = StackTop, I = $FE and fills ImTable $FE00-$FF00 with $FF; writes JR (ImJr $FFFF = $18) and JP Interrupt $9226 at ImJump $FFF4, then IM 2. Clears the first attribute of each zone set ($EF00, $6300, $6C00, $7500). KempstonTest $9F62 sets ControlMethod $A13A to 0 (Kempston) when an interface answers. Then JP GameStart $CBF9.
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$915B c NewGame ; A new game: Matt in room 0, full energy, empty masks, the pick-ups and the maps restored
> Room 0, screen 0 (RoomNumber $950A, RoomScreen $950D); Energy $AEA6 = $FF; Matt (Objects $A43F) at x $48, y $28, state $0B, facing right; clears bit 7 (taken) of every PickupTable $950E record; empties the four MaskSlots $AF2B and selects the first; ShowMaskName EMPTY; turns the map blocks $2B back to $12 and $47 back to $1B in RoomMaps $7600-$84FF (so the maps' own $2B, room 5 screen 0 and room 6 screen 2, become turrets too after the first new game: rzx-16000 frame 3194); clears the end-of-level and effect flags and the Score $AE41. BuildTables $A860 makes the sprite tables first. Ends in DrawRoom $A89D and PasswordPods $ACBC.
> Witness: L1 21 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x8).
$9208 c HangLoop ; Never run: DI, then flash the border forever (the kind-0 slot of ObjectJumps $C326 jumps here)
> XOR 7, OUT ($FE), JP HangLoop. Known only from the code.
$9210 BorderFlash ; never run: flash the border BC times
$9222 b TuneRequest ; The tune to start (1-4; 0 none), read by Interrupt on a 128K
$9223 StopRequest ; non-zero: MusicStop $C00A at the next interrupt; the game never writes it, its loaded $FF makes the first 128K interrupt call MusicStop once (c1)
$9224 FrameCounter ; counted up by every interrupt; no instruction reads it
$9225 BorderColour ; sent to $FE by every interrupt
@module interrupt ; The interrupt and the main loop
@about The game runs free in its main loop MainLoop $CC03 (2.5-5.4 frames a pass, no HALT); everything that must keep time runs in the interrupt Interrupt $9226: the key reading (in the menu MenuInterrupt $9899), the AY music and effects on a 128K or the beeper effect on a 48K, the message scroller and the BREAK check.
$9226 c Interrupt ; The IM 2 handler (via ImJump $FFF4): keys or menu, music and effects, scroller, BREAK
> Saves every register; FrameCounter $9224 + 1, OUT BorderColour. In play (MenuFlag $970E = 0) CheatCheck $BB4C; in the menu MenuInterrupt $9899. On a 128K (MachineFlag $FFFE = 0): pages RAM 4 ($7FFD = $14), starts TuneRequest $9222 (MusicStart) or StopRequest $9223 (MusicStop), runs StopEffects $946F and StartEffects $9421, MusicPlay $C003; in the menu (NotInPlay $970D) it restarts tune 1 when MusicTune ends; pages RAM 0 back ($10). On a 48K: StopBeeper $949F and BeeperTick $94C8. In play: Scroller $AF82, and CAPS SHIFT + SPACE (BREAK) aborts to GameStart $CBF9.
> Witness: L1 63268 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x10).
$92C3 b RandomSeed ; Random's three bytes of state
$92C6 c Random ; A = a pseudo-random byte from RandomSeed and R
> Witness: L1 100334 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x10).
$92E0 b EffectTable 14 ; The 18 sound effects, 14 bytes each: the AY channel data, the channel choice (+$0A), the beeper pitch and length
> PlayEffect $93DC picks record A; on a 128K bytes +$0B-+$0D go to the effect channel blocks of the player, on a 48K the record drives BeeperTick $94C8. The CSV is src/res/tables/effects.csv.
@res tables/effects.bin
$93DC c PlayEffect ; Start sound effect A: an AY channel slot on a 128K, the beeper on a 48K
> 128K: record + $0A picks the slot (1 EffectSlotA $941B, 2 $941D, else $941F) that StartEffects $9421 reads at the next interrupt. 48K: BeeperStart $94AF.
> Witness: L1 638 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x9).
$941B b EffectSlots ; Three slots of (flag, record) for channels A, B and C
$9421 c StartEffects ; Interrupt, 128K: hand each waiting effect to the AY player (EffectStart with IX = the channel block)
> Witness: L1 26094 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2).
$946C b EffectStops ; Three flags: stop the effect of channel A, B, C at the next interrupt
$946F c StopEffects ; Interrupt, 128K: silence each channel whose EffectStops flag is set (writes the player's block +6)
> Channel C's test is inverted (RET NZ at $9493): it zeroes channel C's hold every interrupt while its flag is clear and does nothing when it is set. Inaudible: channel C's envelopes end by themselves (docs/09-sound.md, 9.9).
> Witness: L1 26094 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2).
$949F c StopBeeper ; Interrupt, 48K: the beeper's version of StopEffects
> Witness: L1 37174 (rzx- x10).
$94AB b BeeperState ; The beeper effect: count, pitch, and the record pointer at $94AE that BeeperStart's own first instruction overwrites
> BeeperStart at $94AF begins with the byte $DD of LD ($94AE),IX: the instruction stores the record's address over $94AE-$94AF, its own prefix. After the first effect the byte at $94AF is the record's high byte, so later calls run it as another instruction (SUB D or SUB E for the records at $92xx-$93xx) and then LD ($94AE),HL at $94B0: the store still happens. mkgame keeps $94AB-$94AF as data and the code from $94B0 (known from the code and the 48K recording work/stage2/rec/c48).
$94AE BeeperRecord ; the record pointer (its high byte is BeeperStart's first byte)
$94B0 c BeeperStart ; 48K: LD ($94AE),HL and the effect's count and pitch (entered at $94AF)
> Witness: L1 541 (rzx- x9).
$94C3 c BeeperOff ; Never run: clear the beeper count
> Known only from the code.
$94C8 c BeeperTick ; Interrupt, 48K: one burst of the beeper effect on bits 3-4 of port $FE
> The low half of the period is not reloaded: the JR NZ at $9505 has no DEC before it, so the low half never waits (docs/09-sound.md, 9.7 and 9.9).
> Witness: L1 37174 (rzx- x10).
@module rooms
$950A b RoomNumber ; The room, 0-15
$950B RoomRecord ; the room's RoomTable record
$950D RoomScreen ; 8 x the screen (0-5): the map column of the screen's left edge
$950E b PickupTable 4 ; The 11 masks lying in the rooms, 4 bytes each [room + bit 7 taken, mask kind, x, y], $FF at the end
> PlacePickupsInScreen $A9BE shows the records of the room's screen that are not taken; CheckPickups $B126 sets bit 7 when Matt takes one; NewGame clears the bits. Eleven pick-ups; kinds 2, 3, 9 and 10 (ULTRA FLASH, MIRAGE, LAVA SHOT, STREAMER) are in no record and cannot be had in play. Also src/res/tables/pickups.csv.
@res tables/pickups.bin
$953B b RoomTable 12 ; 16 records of 12 bytes: left, right, pod, exit 3, zone, arrival, an enemy kind a screen
> Bytes: 0 the room to the left, 1 to the right ($FF none), 2 the pod's destination (Teleport $B6B3), 3 an exit read only by the never-run ExitByte3 $B6D8, 4 the zone, 5 the arrival place after a pod: x = (b & $1F) x 4 + $40, RoomScreen = (b & $E0) / 4, 6-11 one enemy kind (EnemyKind $BFB0) for each of the six screens (DrawRoom $A89D). The table is also src/res/tables/rooms.csv (tools/res_formats.py writes it from these bytes).
@res tables/rooms.bin
$95FB b Font 5 ; 5-row glyphs: A-Z, then 0-9 at $967D, '.' $96AF, ':' $96B4, space $96B9
@res font/font5.bin
$96BE c CharGlyph ; HL = the 5-byte glyph of character A (letters, digits, '.', ':', space)
> Witness: L1 40146 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x10).
$970D b NotInPlay ; $FF in the menu and the death sequence: no scroller, no BREAK, the menu tune loops
$970E MenuFlag ; non-zero: Interrupt runs MenuInterrupt instead of CheatCheck
$9710 HudSaved ; $FF as loaded: the first Menu skips SaveHud (PlayPanel $F600 still holds the loaded panel); Menu then sets 0, so every later Menu copies the screen's panel back to $F600 (BuildTables overwrote it)
$9711 MenuColours ; 16 colours for the menu's lit icon and bars
$9721 MenuColourCount ; the colour cycle's step
@module menu ; The menu, the controls, DEFINE KEYS, the password
@about Menu $9723 wipes the screen, draws the logo and the 15 menu strings, and waits in MenuLoop $9775 for 1-4 (Kempston, Interface 2, Cursor, keyboard), K (DEFINE KEYS), P (ENTER PASSWORD) or fire (start). The interrupt animates the logo and colours in MenuInterrupt $9899.
$9723 c Menu ; The menu: wipe, logo, strings; MenuLoop until fire, then the play screen's panel and tune 3
> Witness: L1 19 (c1, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x8).
$9775 MenuLoop ; draw the strings and the lit icon, HALT, read a key
$984D c MenuWipe ; Wipe the attributes diagonally (PokeAttr)
> Witness: L1 19 (c1, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x8).
$985A c MenuWipeStep ; One diagonal of the wipe
> Witness: L1 1330 (c1, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x8).
$9876 c PokeAttr ; Set the attribute at row D, column E to A when they are on the screen
> Witness: L1 323612 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x9).
$9899 c MenuInterrupt ; The menu's interrupt: the logo's raster colours, the lit control icon, the border bars, the colour scroll
> Witness: L1 16790 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x9).
$992F c ClearScreen ; Clear the bitmap and the attributes
> Witness: L1 19 (c1, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x8).
$9951 c LogoRaster ; Colour the logo line by line (LDI from the buffer at $F0CA in time with the beam)
> Witness: L1 16790 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x9).
$999E c ScreenAddr ; HL = the screen address of character row D, column E
> Witness: L1 1013 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x9).
$99B8 c DrawGraphic ; Draw B x C characters from HL at row D, column E
> Witness: L1 351 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x9).
$99F0 b MenuLogo 8 ; The menu's logo, 10 x 6 characters (Menu draws it at row 0, column 11)
@res screens/menu-logo.bin
$9BD0 b MenuBadge 8 ; A 2 x 1 picture drawn at row 6, column 19
@res screens/menu-badge.bin
$9BE0 b MenuBanner 8 ; A 12 x 2 picture drawn at row 22, column 10
@res screens/menu-banner.bin
$9CA0 c SaveHud ; Keep screen rows 18-23 at $F600 and their attributes at $FC64 (the play panel, restored at the start)
> Witness: L1 18 (door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x8).
$9CBF c PrintString ; Print the bit-7-terminated string at HL at row D, column E
> Witness: L1 601 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x8).
$9CD9 c PrintChar ; Print character A (5-row glyph, attribute $47)
> Witness: L1 37418 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x10).
$9D01 b ControlIconPlaces ; The menu rows and columns of the lit control icons
$9D16 Hiscore ; the high score, 4 BCD bytes
$9D1A c DrawMenu ; The 15 menu strings, the high score and the control icons
> Witness: L1 39 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x8).
$9D6C t MenuStrings ; The 15 menu strings: two place bytes (column, then row: $18, $09 for PROGRAM), the text with bit 7 on the last character
> Includes "P.ENTER PASSWOID" as the bytes have it (the original's typo; the screen shows it, work/stage1/c1).
@res texts/menu.bin
$9E10 c ClearMenuArea ; Clear the menu's text area
> Witness: L1 12 (c1, cheat, play2).
$9E3B c DefineKeys ; DEFINE KEYS: FIRE, UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, each a key not taken yet
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$9E7B c AskKey ; Wait for a key that is not one of the keys chosen so far
> Witness: L1 5 (c1).
$9E90 t DefinePrompts ; "FIRE", "UP", "DOWN", "LEFT", "RIGHT" and "Press"
$9EAF c ColourScroll ; The menu's colour bars, a random sequence a cycle
> Witness: L1 16815 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x9).
$9ED3 b ColourSequences ; The colour sequences of ColourScroll
$9F62 c KempstonTest ; Z when port $1F reads with bits 5-7 clear 256 times (a Kempston interface)
> Witness: L1 5 (c1, play2, rzx-08000, rzx-28000).
$9F6D b PasswordFlags ; MAYHEM, TRANSMOGRIFY, VALKYR entered; $9F70 PETALS OF DOOM (all three)
$9F71 PasswordBuffer ; the 16 key codes typed, 0 at the end
$9F82 c EnterPassword ; ENTER PASSWORD: 16 keys, compared with the four passwords (key codes)
> Each matching password sets its flag; PETALS OF DOOM sets $9F70 only when the other three are set (the AND at $9FE9-$9FF2). Witness: work/stage2/rec/play2 types the four passwords in order: each compare matches once, the four flags are written once each, and the next NewGame's PasswordPods $ACBC writes the open blocks $1E/$1F for all four doors (ACD1 run 4 times a call, ACC9 never). The flags let Matt into a door (MattWalk $B48D-$B4BB: room 0, screen 5, standing on character $1C, down held).
> Witness: L1 5 (cheat, play2).
$9FF9 t PasswordDots ; The 16 dots EnterPassword prints at row $0A, column $08
$A009 b Passwords ; MAYHEM, TRANSMOGRIFY, VALKYR, PETALS OF DOOM as key codes, each 0-terminated
> Key code = row x 16 + bit (row 0 = port $FEFE ... row 7 = $7FFE). src/res/texts/passwords.txt has them as letters.
@res texts/passwords.bin
$A033 c StringMatch ; Z when the buffer at HL equals the 0-terminated code string at DE
> Witness: L1 20 (cheat, play2).
$A040 c ScreenWipe ; Close the screen from the top and the bottom, one line pair a HALT (88 steps)
> Witness: L1 21 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x8).
$A076 c ClearLine ; Clear one pixel line
> Witness: L1 3717 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x8).
$A081 b KeysIf2 ; Interface 2 keys (fire, up, down, left, right): 0 9 8 6 7
$A086 KeysCursor ; Cursor keys: 0 7 6 5 8
$A08B KeysUser ; the keyboard set (DEFINE KEYS): SPACE P L Q W as loaded
$A090 c KeyPressed ; NZ when key code A is down (patches its own port and bit)
> Witness: L1 103894 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x10).
$A0B2 c ScanKeyboard ; The first key down as a key code, or none
> Witness: L1 34726 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x9).
$A0C9 c ReadKeyCode ; A key code from ScanKeyboard
> Witness: L1 34726 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x9).
$A0E5 c WaitKey ; Wait for a key: A the character, A' the key code
> Witness: L1 2470 (c1, cheat, play2).
$A0F1 b KeyChars ; The 40 keys' characters, by key code
$A119 c KeyCodeToChar ; A = the character of key code A
> Witness: L1 271 (c1, cheat, door, door3, play2, rzx- x5).
$A138 b Controls ; this pass's controls: bit 0 right, 1 left, 2 down, 3 up, 4 fire
$A139 ControlsLast ; the last pass's
$A13A ControlMethod ; 0 Kempston, 1 Interface 2, 2 Cursor, 3 keyboard
$A13B c ReadControls ; Controls from the Kempston port or the chosen keys; right beats left, down beats up
> Witness: L1 27243 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x10).
$A150 b KeysNow ; The five keys in use (copied from KeysIf2, KeysCursor or KeysUser)
@module renderer ; The renderer: zone swapping, the dirty map, the sprites drawn as characters
@about Everything on the play area is characters. The 32 x 20 character map at $F080 (rows 2-19 shown, from $F0C0) names a character of the live zone; the dirty map $F3C0-$F5FF marks each cell to redraw (1 the zone character from ZoneChars $E000 / ZoneAttrs $EF00, 2 a sprite character from $E800 / $EE00). A sprite is drawn by allocating fresh characters from $E800 up, copying the backgrounds into them and ORing the masked, shifted picture in (DrawObject $A56F); FlushDirty $A1F0 then puts the dirty cells on the screen. Characters $EA and up of a zone are foreground and are never drawn over.
$A194 b ZoneSlots ; ZoneSlots[0] the live zone, [1-3] the zones parked at $5B00, $6400, $6D00
$A198 c SwapZone ; Make zone A live: swap its parked $900 bytes with ZoneChars/ZoneAttrs, under DI
> Also writes TurretStems $A1EC[zone] into TurretStem $C26E. Witness: L1 86 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x9); the per-frame trace of a room change is in work/stage2/NOTES.md.
$A1EC b TurretStems ; One character a zone: the stem KindTurret draws under a turret (copied to TurretStem $C26E)
$A1F0 c FlushDirty ; Draw every dirty cell (from $F5FF down to the sentinel $F3BF) and clear its mark
> Witness: L1 15472 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x9).
$A253 b PickupSaves ; The backgrounds kept under the pick-up icons
$A2CB PickupSavePtr ; the next free save
$A2CD NextSpriteChar ; the next free sprite character
$A2CE FirstSpriteChar ; the first sprite character of this pass
$A2CF DissolveCount ; non-zero: Matt is drawn dissolved (pods, penetrator, death)
$A2D0 c DrawObjects ; The last step of a pass: place pick-ups, draw the 8 objects, flush, restore the backgrounds
> Witness: L1 15361 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x9).
$A349 c SelectFrame ; The object's frame address from its mode (+$19), animation (+$18) and mask (+$1A); Matt's from his state and x
> Witness: L1 104259 (c1, cheat, door, door3, kind6, masks, play2, rzx- x9).
