$CC5C b PassBcd ; A BCD pass counter (bit 0 times PENETRATOR's charges and the turret's bob)
$CC5D s PassBcdSpare ; 35 zero bytes no routine reads
@module sprites ; The pictures: control icons, Matt, the enemies, digits, mask icons
@about Every moving picture is a run of characters (8 bytes each) stored column by column: a frame w characters wide and h high is w x h x 8 bytes, character (column c, row r) at 8 x (c x h + r). An object's frame is its picture +$16/+$17 + (animation & mask) x the frame size of its mode (SelectFrame $A349: modes 2-3 48 bytes, 4 32, 5 8, 6 one frame, 7 72). DrawObject $A56F makes the mask and the mirror image at run time, so no masks are stored. The PNGs are 1-bit, frames side by side (src/res/sprites/README.md).
$CC80 b ControlIcons 8 ; Seven 2 x 2 pictures: the four control icons of the menu and three more
> DrawMenu $9D1A draws the icons of the four control methods; the lit one blinks in MenuInterrupt. Witness: c1 menu.
@res sprites/control-icons.bin
$CD60 b MattRun 8 ; Matt running: 8 frames of 4 x 4 characters (32 x 32 pixels)
> SelectFrame picks frame ((x / 4) & 7), backwards when he faces left. Witness: every pass of play (c1).
@res sprites/matt-run.bin
$D160 b MattJump 8 ; Matt jumping or falling (states 8, 10, 12), 4 x 4
@res sprites/matt-jump.bin
$D1E0 b MattCrouch 8 ; Matt crouching (state 4), 4 x 4
@res sprites/matt-crouch.bin
$D260 b SpriteFaller 8 ; Enemy kinds 1 and 12 (templates $BE3B, $BE9B): 4 frames of 2 x 2
@res sprites/faller.bin
$D2E0 b SpriteFlyer 8 ; Enemy kind 2 ($BE47): 4 frames of 3 x 2
@res sprites/flyer.bin
$D3A0 b Digits 8 ; The score digits 0-9, 1 x 2 characters (16 bytes) each (DrawDigit $AE78)
@res sprites/digits.bin
$D440 b SpriteExplosion 8 ; The explosion ($BEFB): 4 frames of 2 x 2
@res sprites/explosion.bin
$D4C0 b SpriteExplosion2 8 ; The big explosion ($BF07): 4 frames of 3 x 2
@res sprites/explosion-big.bin
$D580 b MaskIcons 8 ; The 11 mask icons (EMPTY and the ten masks), 2 x 2 each (DrawIcon $B024, PlacePickup $A9DA)
@res sprites/mask-icons.bin
$D6E0 b SpriteShots 8 ; Matt's shots: 6 frames of 2 x 2, one a mask kind 5-10 (FireMask sets the animation to kind - 5)
@res sprites/shots.bin
$D7A0 b SpriteTurret 8 ; The turret (kind 4, $BE53): 4 frames of 3 x 2
@res sprites/turret.bin
$D860 b SpriteTurretShot 8 ; The turret's shot (kind 5, $BE5F): 8 frames of 1 x 1
@res sprites/turret-shot.bin
$D8A0 b SpriteWave 8 ; The wave flyer (kind 6, $BE6B): 6 frames of 2 x 2
@res sprites/wave.bin
$D960 b SpriteWalker 8 ; The walker (kind 7, $BE77): 4 frames of 2 x 2
@res sprites/walker.bin
$D9E0 b SpriteChaser 8 ; The chaser (kind 8, $BE83): one picture of 8 x 3
@res sprites/chaser.bin
$DAA0 b SpriteKind16 8 ; Kind 16's picture ($BE8F, spawned only by a POKE in work/stage2/rec/kind6): 4 frames of 2 x 3
@res sprites/kind16.bin
$DB60 b SpriteBig 8 ; One 4 x 3 picture ($BECB)
@res sprites/big.bin
$DBC0 b SpriteGuard 8 ; The guard (kind 13, $BEA7): one picture of 4 x 4
@res sprites/guard.bin
$DC40 b SpritePart1 8 ; Kind 18's picture ($BF13): 4 frames of 3 x 3
@res sprites/part1.bin
$DD60 b SpritePart2 8 ; Kind 19's picture ($BF1F): 4 frames of 3 x 3
@res sprites/part2.bin
$DE80 b SpriteSmall1 8 ; Three 2 x 2 pictures ($BED7, $BEE3, $BEEF)
@res sprites/small.bin
$DEE0 b SpriteBoss 8 ; The boss (kind 14, $BEB3): one picture of 4 x 4
