@module buffers ; The live zone, the sprite characters and the buffers, with what the loader leaves in them
@about $DF80-$FDFF are work space at run time. As loaded they hold zone 0's set (live), zone 1's first characters and attributes (copied down by GameEntry), and the play panel that the first game start draws; the rest are leftovers that are overwritten before any read (known only from the code).
$DF80 s DissolveBuffer ; 128 bytes: Dissolve's frame
$E000 b ZoneChars 8 ; The live zone's 256 characters: zone 0's as loaded
@res charsets/zone0.bin
$E800 b SpriteChars 8 ; The sprite characters DrawObject allocates; as loaded 1536 bytes of leftovers
> DrawObject $A56F writes every sprite character from $E800 up before FlushDirty reads it; the loaded bytes are never read (known only from the code).
@res leftovers/e800.bin
$EE00 b Zone1Attrs 16 ; Zone 1's attributes, copied to $6300 by GameEntry; then the sprite characters' attributes
@res charsets/zone1-attr.bin
$EF00 b ZoneAttrs 16 ; The live zone's attributes (bit 7 solid): zone 0's as loaded
@res charsets/zone0-attr.bin
$F000 b Zone1CharsLow 8 ; Zone 1's characters 0-159, copied to $5B00 by GameEntry; then the masks, the character map ($F080) and the dirty map ($F3C0)
$F000 MaskBuffer ; at run time: the sprite mask (MakeMask $A777) and DrawObject's work space, $F000-$F07F
$F080 CharMap ; at run time: the character map, 32 x 20 character codes; row 2 ($F0C0) is screen row 0
$F300 MirrorBuffer ; at run time: MirrorFrame's mirrored frame
$F3C0 DirtyMap ; at run time: the dirty marks, 32 x 18, one a shown cell (1 the zone character, 2 a sprite character), to $F5FF
@res charsets/zone1-low.bin
$F500 b LeftoverF500 16 ; 256 bytes of leftovers, cleared as the dirty map before any read
@res leftovers/f500.bin
$F600 b PlayPanel 8 ; The play panel (rows 18-23, 32 x 6 characters), drawn by Menu at the first start; then BuildTables' tables
$F600 BitReverse ; at run time: BuildTables' bit-reverse table (MirrorFrame)
$F700 Dilate ; at run time: the dilate table of MakeMask
$F800 ShiftTables ; at run time: three page pairs, each byte shifted 2, 4 or 6 pixels and the bits pushed out, to $FDFF
@res screens/panel.bin
$FC00 b LeftoverFC00 16 ; 100 bytes between the panel and its attributes (overwritten by BuildTables)
@res leftovers/fc00.bin
$FC64 b PanelAttrs 32 ; The panel's attributes, 6 rows of 32
@res screens/panel-attr.bin
$FD24 b LeftoverFD24 16 ; 220 bytes of leftovers, overwritten by BuildTables' shift tables
@res leftovers/fd24.bin
